      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y={x}^{2}-4x-7.$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=1$ and $b=-4$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-4)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$",
